# Agentic AI Engineer - Intern

# Welcome!

Thank you for your interest in the Agentic AI Engineer role.
As a final. year student at CIT, Coimbatore, you have already built a strong technical foundation. This take-home assignment is designed to evaluate your ability to bridge that academic knowledge with real-world AI engineering. We want to see how you string together various AI agents, APIs, and algorithms to build a cohesive, automated workflow. We are looking for product sense, technical execution, and your ability to leverage AI tools creatively.

## 🎯 The Objective

Your task is to build a full-stack, AI-powered conversational web application called **"The Lenny Growth Assistant."**

This application will ingest transcripts from *Lenny's Podcast*, allow users to ask complex Q&A questions, and generate highly specific, formatted content based on that knowledge. Furthermore, the application must be able to generate code and markdown artifacts and render them natively within the UI—creating an immersive, ChatGPT-like workspace.

## ⚙️ Core Requirements & Workflow

Your application pipeline must perform the following steps and adhere to these constraints:

### 1. API & Session Management (FastAPI)

- **Backend Framework:** You must build the backend API using FastAPI.
- **Agent Integration:** Build the API on top of the Anthropic Claude SDK or Pi Coding Agent.
- **Session Handling:** The API must allow the user to start **new chat sessions**, exactly how the "New Chat" feature works in ChatGPT. Each session must maintain its own context.
- **Database:** All conversations, session IDs, and user metadata must be persistently stored in a postgres database. You can choose either Supabase or Railway

### 2. Flexible LLM Configuration (Cloud & Local)

Your system must have a configuration layer that allows the user to easily switch the underlying LLM engine:

- **Cloud LLM:** Integration with a cloud provider (e.g., Anthropic Claude, OpenAI).
- **Local LLM (Mandatory for Demo):** For the local demo submission, you **must** configure the application to run using a local LLM via Ollama. You may use any model that runs comfortably on your laptop.

### 3. Knowledge Base

- **Data Source:** Transcripts from *Lenny's Podcast/Newsletter* https://github.com/ChatPRD/lennys-podcast-transcripts.

### **4a. Task: Conversational Chatbot on the transcripts**

- **Q&A Agent:** Implement a system (RAG / long-context prompting) that allows the user to ask product management and growth questions. The agent must answer *strictly* using the insights from Lenny's transcripts.

### 4b. Task: Content Generation (Ship30for30 Style)

- The agent must feature a specific "Skill" or tool that allows it to synthesize answers into the **Ship30for30 style**. We expect you to read this and know how to write such a content. The skill should be generated.
- *Requirement:* The output should be formatted as an "Essay" (approx. 1250 words, strong hook, heavily formatted with bullet points, bold text for skimmability, and a clear takeaway).

### 4c. Task: Artifact Generation & Viewer UI

- When prompted, the AI must be able to generate **Artefacts** (Markdown documents or complete HTML/CSS snippets) based on the conversation context.
- **In-App Viewer:** Your frontend application must feature an "Artifact Viewer" (similar to Claude's Artifacts). When the AI generates HTML/CSS or Markdown, the application should not just show the raw code; it should render the actual UI component or stylized document side-by-side with the chat. You should build this feature within the app (not redirect to external browser or app).

